  - Mechanistic Interpretability
  - SwiGLU
  - Finite State Machine
  - Large Language Models
abstract: >-
  We identify that the failure of traditional mid-layer weight editing and activation steering in multi-step autoregressive generation stems from KV-Cache Autoregressive Drift: control signals injected into intermediate layers pollute downstream KV caches across subsequent generation steps. By exploiting the topological uniqueness of the terminal MLP layer (Layer L-1, which executes strictly after all self-attention KV cache writes) together with bfloat16 SiLU floating-point underflow in dormant SwiGLU neurons and a Whitened Unembedding Dual Basis, we compile a complete three-stage dialectical verification circuit and branching DAG finite state machine directly into ~0.035% of model weights in 30 seconds with zero gradient descent. Across 3,780 unfiltered 3-turn adversarial dialogues on Qwen3-8B and Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, our method passes 12/12 paired bootstrap 95% confidence interval tests and outperforms reinforcement learning (SelfD-RL, arXiv:2611.17563) without reward-hacking stubbornness.
